    "intake_lift_source": "[AS] shape: the A25A's digitised SAE 2019-01-0249 Fig. 11 curves, x stretched by 1.289878 (intake) / 1.292750 (exhaust) so the 1 mm crossings land on IVO 31.0 / IVC 281.9 and EVO 478.2 / EVC 729.1 deg at zero cam phase ([D] IVC0 281.9 / EVO0 478.2 deg (zero cam phase, 1 mm [AS]) from the workbook's EPA Atkinson-ratio column (EVO0/IVC0 fit over all rows, stroke 100 mm and l/r 3.0 [AS], rms ratio error 0.0013); ov0 -22.0 [D] exact from the overlap column. The 1 mm durations are therefore ~251 deg each. Cooled external EGR (part of the real knock strategy) is NOT in the cycle model.); lift x 1.017143 (bore ratio, L/D held).",
